{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1464 (owner 2026-10-30): WHAT A CONVERSATION'S SESSION ROWS DO ×4, a thread's Conversation and a team agent's conversation alike (session-thread.json rows). threadRowAction({type, sessionId, rootId, state, blocked, answered}): a row of type `session` (a `session` / `thread_started` card, an escalated ask's card; sessionId = its card's), `report` (its xref's session) or `event` (its `sessionId`, null when the card names none or it has not synced) naming a session OTHER than the conversation's own root does something; anything else, or a row about the root itself, does NOTHING (`none`: no chevron, no hover, no press). `expand`: a `session` row whose state (session-card.json) is `needs_you` and NOT behind a flag (`blocked` = the session's `blocked` is set: a usage wall, not picked up, stuck; those have no card) expands IN PLACE: under THE session card (its chevron turns down; a tap collapses it) sits THE question / plan card of that session (`sessionWaitingCard`, the same card a thread renders, answerable there via sessions.answer), its header carrying `copy.openChat` (testIds.openChat) which opens the session. While the card has not synced the card slot is the skeleton line. Once the viewer answered it (client-held `answered`) the row collapses and, while the session is neither `needs_you` again nor `done`, reads the quiet `copy.answered` (`kindWord`, tone `muted`) instead of its state word; needing you again expands again. `open`: every other row naming a session opens THAT session by inbox-route.json `sessionTarget` (the viewer's own agent conversation root = the agent's page, a thread root = its thread, a thread's child = in its thread, anything else under an agent = its own session screen); a session of the SAME thread opens in place. chevron = action != none: a session card's trailing chevron, a `Report from` line's, an event line's (the muted line becomes a button: hover = foreground, press = the pressed wash). sessionWaitingCard(sessionId, messages) = that session's NEWEST (createdAt, ties by the higher id) waiting `question` (answeredAt null) or `plan` (no decision; `superseded` is a decision) message id, else null. Mirrors: TS src/thread-row-action.ts, desktop `domain::thread_row_action`, iOS ExpCore `ThreadRowAction.swift`, Android `domain/ThreadRowAction.kt`; each replays `cases` and `waitingCases` comparing the WHOLE expected object.",
